    "phenomenon": "Gateway returns HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout while application reports EACCES permission denied for same correlation ID",
    "causal_chain": "The gateway timed out waiting for a response from the application layer, which itself failed with EACCES (permission denied). This suggests the application attempted an operation it lacked permissions to perform\u2014possibly file access, system call, or inter-process communication\u2014and did not respond in time, causing the gateway to timeout. The shared correlation ID links both failures, indicating they originate from the same request flow.",
    "alternatives": "EACCES could reflect misconfigured filesystem or container runtime permissions; 504 could stem from upstream dependency latency or deadlock\u2014not necessarily the same root cause. Both errors may be coincident but independent.",
